                <head><seg type="margin">[668]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton, Secretary of State, to Mr. Hall, district attorney.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1850-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26,
                        1850</date>.</dateline>
                <p>Your several notes of yesterday’s date were received to-day. In reply to that
                    part of your note dated yesterday, at 3½ p.m., I am directed to state that you
                    have full authority from the President to act under the eighth section of the
                    act of 20th April, 1818, in order to seize and detain munitions of war intended
                    to be used in aid of the Cuban expedition. It is expected by the President that
                    you will, as far as in your power, strictly execute the law.</p>
            </div>
